Package: matchdb
Title: A Provenanced Disambiguation Database for Nonprofit Record Linkage
Version: 0.1.1.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Jesse", "Lecy", email = "jdlecy@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Builds and distributes the reference side of nonprofit record
    linkage: the universe of known EIN-to-name and EIN-to-address observations
    from the IRS Business Master File, Form 990 Schedule I grant disclosures,
    and other sources, each row carrying its provenance. Names and addresses are
    stored long, one row per observed variant, normalized once and selected at
    compile time by layer (which EINs exist) and variant class (which observed
    strings for them). Compiled references are published as versioned artifacts
    stamped with the normalizer signature they were built against, so a cached
    artifact cannot be silently used with a normalizer that has since changed.
    Normalization comes from 'npnormalize'; the linkage machinery itself
    lives in 'npmatch'.
